@packages/sigilc/compiler.sigil from SigilSemanticCompiler import { SourceTrees }

component SigilSourceIdentity {
  goal {
    Capture selected files as stable *SourceIdentity* values for SourceTrees
    and implementation alignment.
  }

  constraints {
    SourceIdentity A source identity uses its normalized workspace-relative
    path and *BLAKE3* content checksum. Captured bytes must match a fresh
    filesystem checksum. File identity excludes neighboring sources, selection
    order, and model data.
  }

  cases {
    *FocusedSelection* Selecting *explicit files* leaves unrelated trees
    unread. Repeated paths contribute one file row, and a file-only selection
    has the same identity as an equivalent directory selection.

    SourceIdentity Editing one imported source changes that source row and the
    selected union identity; the unchanged importer's own source identity stays
    stable. Retained captured bytes stay unchanged after a later live edit.
  }

  interface {
    *SemanticInputs* Bind each SourceIdentity to its own parsed tree and resolved
    component interfaces, plus applicable configuration and glossary bytes or their
    absence. A dependency's private edit does not change the importer's basis
    when its interface is unchanged. An unresolved import invalidates its own
    source. Keep production metadata outside source identity.

    *CompilerInputSelection* Select workspace-relative paths and directories
    with include and exclude globs. Support any file extension, omit internal
    and configured vendor trees, and reject accidental empty selection.
    Explicit file selection filters before hashing and does not traverse
    unrelated trees. Refuse symlink crossings, non-regular files, and sources
    that change while read.
  }
}
